ussion: Proposal 1: create a new RAN1-led technical specification to specify channel access mechanisms for unlicensed and shared spectrum, taking the Rel-13/14/15 contents of section 15 of 36.213. Consider the 37 spec series. Proposal 2: create new RAN4 specifications for including the unlicensed band definition, i.e. band 46, and all the requirements related to LBT mechanism for both BS and UE, including channel access procedures, RRM for frame structure 3, and demodulation tests for LAA/eLAA. Consider the 37 spec series. RAN chair: changes REL-13 onwards or REL-15 onwards? Huawei: REL-15 onwards RAN chair: may give problems with mirror CRs Samsung: impact on NR specs? Huawei: that's why we suggest 37 series specs CableLabs: band 49 is under discussion, is the time right to do this now? Ericsson: 37 series includes MSR specs which we forgot for IMT-2020 submission RAN chair: this is not the reason why 37 series is proposed here Ericsson: 36.300 also has also LAA aspects RAN chair: which WGs? Huawei: RAN1 and RAN4 RAN chair: so we will come back at RAN #78 how to do this in detail MCC: new WID for this? Huawei: no, we will revise WID for LTE_unlic and do the changes under this WI conclusion: revised WID for LTE_unlic will be provided to RAN #78 how to change REL-15 specs (no CRs for this to RAN #78) and which new REL-15 37 series specs will be introduced for this Decision: The document was noted. RP-171839 Status report of WI: Core part: Further video enhancements for LTE; rapporteur: CMCC Source: RAN2 Abstract: Related WID: RP-171392 Discussion: conclusion: approved: Core: 35%, Dec.17 Decision: The document was noted. RP-171566 Status report of WI Core part: Quality of Experience (QoE) Measurement Collection for streaming services in E-UTRAN; rapporteur: China Unicom Source: RAN2 Discussion: conclusion: approved: 45%, Dec.17 Decision: The document was noted. RP-171859 Status report for WI: Enhancing LTE CA utilization; rapporteur: Nokia Source: RAN2 Discussion: conclusion: approved: Core: 22%, June 18; Perf.: 0%, Dec.18 Decision: The document was noted.

